# VARS: a check of Studio's 128 variables (make test-vars). Each has its
# own value: A is 1 and A1 5 (variable 8), H15 (127, the last) is 7, B2
# (17) is A1 + H15 = 12, C12 (98) counts to 10 in a loop. It shows
# 1 5 7 12 10.
# Then SAVE VARS and LOAD VARS: all of them to VARS.TXT, five set to 9,
# the row A1..H1 (A1 9) to ROW1.TXT; VARS.TXT back, then ROW1.TXT's
# row, then ROW1.TXT for A..H (none of them in it: nothing changes). The
# second row shows 1 9 7 12 10.
MODE 1
BG 2

START STAGE
SET A 1
SET A1 5
SET H15 7
SET B2 A1
CHANGE B2 H15
SET C12 0
REPEAT 10
  CHANGE C12 1
END
PRINT A 100 100
PRINT A1 140 100
PRINT H15 180 100
PRINT B2 220 100
PRINT C12 260 100
SAVE_VARS "VARS" ALL
SET A 9
SET A1 9
SET H15 9
SET B2 9
SET C12 9
SAVE_VARS "ROW1" A1-H1
LOAD_VARS "VARS" ALL
LOAD_VARS "ROW1.TXT" A1-H1
LOAD_VARS "row1" A-H
PRINT A 100 130
PRINT A1 140 130
PRINT H15 180 130
PRINT B2 220 130
PRINT C12 260 130
